[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Report high-level requirements
UID: FMD-HLR-RPT
VERSION: Issue 1
DATE: 2026-11-20
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Markdown

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @flightmd

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Behaviour of the report item as seen at its interfaces, written from the code as built: the report data model
(`flightmd_core/models/`), scoring, explanations, report assembly, the optional AI summary, flight context
(weather, place name, airframe name), the GPX, KML and PDF exports and the schema export script. Parents are
system requirements (`docs/lifecycle/03-system/system-requirements.sdoc`). Low-level requirements are in
`llr-rpt.sdoc`, the design in `docs/lifecycle/06-design/lld-rpt.md`, the interfaces in
`docs/lifecycle/03-system/icd/icd-report-and-exports.md` and `icd-external-services.md`.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Report data model

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: The report identifies itself and its input
STATEMENT: >>>
A report (`FlightMDReport`) shall carry a `report_id` (a UUID), `schema_version` (`"1.7"`), `file_name`,
`file_size_bytes` (bytes), `generated_at` (UTC, `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`), `processing_time_ms` and, in its
metadata, fields for the SHA-256 of the log (`log_sha256`), the detected format (`source_format`) and a planning
brief SHA-256 (`planning_brief_sha256`). The report item fills `report_id`, `schema_version`, `generated_at` and
`processing_time_ms`; the caller supplies the others.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-020
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-019
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-024

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: What a finding carries
STATEMENT: >>>
A finding (`Finding`) shall carry a category, a severity (`critical`, `warning`, `info`, `good`), a title, a
technical summary, a plain-English text, a recommendation, a confidence held between 0.0 and 1.0 with a level
(`high`, `medium`, `low`), an optional time window in log-relative milliseconds and the same window in seconds,
optional chart data, parameter changes, the rule identifier `kind` and the list of parameter names the finding
touches. A confidence that is not finite shall become 0.0.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: A skipped module is never assessed
STATEMENT: >>>
A module result (`AnalyserResult`) shall carry `skipped`, `skip_reason` and `assessed`. A result with
`skipped` true shall always have `assessed` false, whatever the producer set.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-010

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Scoring

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Overall score is the weighted mean of assessed modules
STATEMENT: >>>
The overall score shall be the mean of the `health_score` values (each held to 0 to 100) of the module results
that are assessed and have a weight above 0, weighted by the module weights, rounded to one decimal place.
Skipped, unassessed and zero-weight modules shall not change it. Each module's own `health_score` is used as the
module computed it.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Nothing assessed gives no score and no grade
STATEMENT: >>>
When no weighted module was assessed (all skipped, all failed, none present, or only zero-weight modules ran)
the score shall be 0.0 with the label `Not assessed` and the grade `-`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-011
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Label and grade come from one band table
STATEMENT: >>>
The label and the letter grade shall both be read from one table of score floors: 90 `Excellent`/`A`, 80
`Good`/`B`, 70 `Caution`/`C`, 60 `Caution`/`D`, 50 `Warning`/`E`, 0 `Critical`/`F`. A score equal to a floor
belongs to that band.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Share of the weight assessed
STATEMENT: >>>
The report shall carry `assessed_fraction`: the weight of the modules that were assessed divided by the total
weight of all registered modules, 0.0 to 1.0, rounded to three decimal places.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-011

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Explanations and summary

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Plain-English text from templates keyed by kind
STATEMENT: >>>
The plain-English text of a finding shall be the fixed template text for its `kind`. The title shall never be
used to choose a template. A finding whose `kind` is absent or has no template (which includes every finding
of the ascent profile module and of a plugin with its own kinds) shall get its technical summary as its
plain-English text.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-013
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: The module's own recommendation is kept
STATEMENT: >>>
A recommendation set by the module shall be kept unchanged. Only when it is empty, or equal to the technical
summary, shall it be replaced: by the template recommendation for the `kind`, else by a fixed text for the
category, else by one fixed default text.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Executive summary from fixed sentences
STATEMENT: >>>
The executive summary shall be built from fixed sentences: the score, label and log duration; the titles of the
critical findings, or else of the warnings, or else a count of minor notes, or else a statement that no anomaly
was detected in the checks that could run; and the display names of the modules that were not assessed. When
the label is `Not assessed` the summary shall instead say that there is no health score and that this is not a
clean bill of health, and shall quote no score.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-010
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-012

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Report assembly

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Findings most severe first
STATEMENT: >>>
The report's `findings` list shall be ordered critical, warning, info, good, and within one severity by
confidence from high to low; findings equal on both keep the order they arrived in.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No system requirement asks for an order. The change sheet's rule that the first recommendation for a parameter
wins depends on this order, and readers of the report see the worst finding first.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
DERIVED: Yes
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: One change-sheet entry per parameter
STATEMENT: >>>
The parameter change sheet shall hold at most one entry per parameter name: the recommendation of the first
finding (in report order) that names it. A later recommendation for the same parameter with a different
direction shall be noted in the kept entry's reason, ending "Review before changing."; a later one with the
same direction is dropped without a note. A recommendation whose current or suggested value is not finite shall
appear neither on its finding nor on the sheet. Building the sheet shall not change the recommendations shown on
the findings.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-015

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Every number in the report is valid JSON
STATEMENT: >>>
Report assembly shall replace NaN and infinity by null in chart data and metadata, drop non-finite key metrics,
set a non-finite module `health_score` or overall score to 0.0, and set a missing or non-finite
`duration_seconds` to 0.0, so that the report serialises with no NaN or infinity.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-019

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-031
STATUS: Active
TITLE: What in a report is not a function of the log
STATEMENT: >>>
Scoring, explanation and assembly shall use no random or learned element. The only report values the report
item produces that differ between two runs on the same log are `report_id` (random UUID), each `Finding.id`
when the module did not set one (random, 8 characters), `generated_at` and `processing_time_ms`. The weather,
the place name and an AI-rewritten summary come from outside services and are not covered by this statement.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test in this item's files analyses one log twice and compares. A review checks that `uuid` and the clock are
used only for the four fields named, and that sorting is stable. `AnalyserResult.processing_ms` also varies; it
is set by the analysers item.
<<<
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-012

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Schema

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Published JSON Schema matches the model
STATEMENT: >>>
The JSON Schema of `FlightMDReport` shall be published as `docs/schema/flightmd-report-<schema_version>.json`
by `scripts/export_schema.py`, and `docs/schema/CHANGELOG.md` shall have a section for the current
`schema_version`. The published file shall equal the schema the model generates.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report, tools
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-019

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Reports of older schema versions still load
STATEMENT: >>>
A report written under an older schema version shall load into the current model: fields added later are
optional or have defaults, the stored `schema_version` is kept, and `Finding.params` is filled from
`param_changes` on load.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-019

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-029
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: The report carries the engine version
STATEMENT: >>>
The report shall carry the version of the analysis engine that produced it.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Not built: `FlightMDReport` has `schema_version` only and no engine version field.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
