[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Exports

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-016
STATUS: Active
TITLE: GPX export of the flight path
STATEMENT: >>>
`generate_gpx` shall return a GPX 1.1 document (UTF-8 bytes) with one track named after the file name and one
track point per `gps_path` point: `lat` and `lon` attributes in decimal degrees to 7 decimal places, `ele` in
metres to 2 decimal places when the point has a finite altitude, and `time` in UTC with milliseconds when the
report has `log_start_utc` and a `gps_path_t_s` list of the same length as the path. With no absolute start
time no `time` element is written. A report with no path gives a valid document with no points. The file name
is XML-escaped.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-022

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-017
STATUS: Active
TITLE: KML export of the flight path
STATEMENT: >>>
`generate_kml` shall return a KML 2.2 document (UTF-8 bytes) named after the file name with the path as one
`LineString` whose coordinates are `lon,lat,alt` (degrees to 7 places, metres to 2 places, altitude 0 when the
point has none), altitude mode `relativeToGround`, and, when the report has per-point time, HDOP or wind, a
hidden folder with one point per path point carrying its UTC time and the values `t_s`, `hdop` and
`wind_speed_ms` that exist for it. A missing reading is left out, not written as 0.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-022

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-018
STATUS: Active
TITLE: PDF report
STATEMENT: >>>
`render_report_pdf` shall return an A4 PDF of a report holding: report id, time of rendering, file name and
size, overall score and label, flight information, the executive summary, every finding (severity, title,
category, confidence, start time, plain-English text, action, technical detail and its parameter changes), the
parameter change sheet, a module summary, a review block and a closing statement that the report is an
engineering analysis aid, not a regulatory or compliance document, and does not replace the judgement of a
qualified engineer. Text from the report is HTML-escaped.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The tests render the HTML only (escaping, no leftover template syntax); no test renders a PDF or checks the
sections. A review reads `templates/report.html` against this statement.
<<<
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-022

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-019
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Airframe record PDF
STATEMENT: >>>
`render_airframe_record_pdf` shall return an A4 PDF for one airframe holding its label, hours since last
maintenance with a due or OK state, a statement that the record is not a regulatory certification, a summary,
the flight history, the maintenance log and the pre-flight checklist, from the values the caller passes.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-030

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-020
STATUS: Active
TITLE: PDF export without the optional packages
STATEMENT: >>>
When Jinja2 or WeasyPrint (or WeasyPrint's system libraries) is not installed, the PDF functions shall raise
`RuntimeError` with a message naming the `flightmd-core[pdf]` extra. Nothing else in the report item needs
those packages.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No system requirement covers the optional install. The caller needs one error type to turn into a message.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
DERIVED: Yes
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-022

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-030
STATUS: Proposed
TITLE: Limits of use on the report and its exports
STATEMENT: >>>
The report data, the PDF and the text exports a person reads shall state that the report is advisory, that a
clean report is not a release to service, and that parameter changes need review and a test flight.
<<<
