[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Optional AI summary

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-021
STATUS: Active
TITLE: The AI may only reword the summary
STATEMENT: >>>
`AIEnhancer.polish_summary` shall take the rule-based summary, the findings and the metadata and return one
string. It shall not change any finding, score or metadata it is given. It shall return the rule-based summary
unchanged when no provider is configured, when the provider call raises any error (which includes a timeout),
when the reply is empty, or when any number in the rule-based summary is missing from the reply.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Tests cover the unconfigured case and a reply that drops a number. The error path and the absence of writes to
the findings are checked by reading `polish_summary`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-023

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-022
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Log-derived text goes to the AI as data
STATEMENT: >>>
Text that came from a log shall reach a prompt only after `clean_text` (control and bidirectional characters
replaced by spaces; the characters `<`, `>`, backtick, braces and square brackets removed; one line; length
capped) and inside `<report>` tags, under a system prompt that tells the model to treat that content as data
and never to follow it.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No system requirement names prompt injection. Finding titles and other strings come from an uploaded file and
could carry instructions aimed at the model.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
DERIVED: Yes
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-023

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-023
STATUS: Active
TITLE: AI is off unless a key for the chosen provider is given
STATEMENT: >>>
`AIEnhancer` shall be configured only when the chosen provider is `groq` (the default) or `anthropic` and a
key for that provider was passed and its client library is installed. Otherwise `is_configured` is false,
`polish_summary` returns its input and `complete` raises `RuntimeError`. `complete` gives the API one
provider-neutral completion call; provider errors pass through it to the caller.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-023

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Flight context

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-024
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Weather of the flight day
STATEMENT: >>>
`fetch_weather` shall return, for a latitude, longitude and UTC start time, a dict with the day's maximum and
minimum temperature (deg C), maximum wind speed (m/s), rain sum (mm) and a description, from the Open-Meteo
archive service or, when that has no data for the day, its forecast service. It shall never raise. With no
position (None or 0,0), no usable date, no network or no data it shall return the same keys with null values
and the description "Weather data unavailable", and it shall never look up a date other than the flight's.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-024

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-025
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Place name
STATEMENT: >>>
`reverse_geocode` shall return a place name at town level ("locality, country") for a latitude and longitude
from OpenStreetMap Nominatim, or `None` for no position (None or 0,0) and on any failure. It shall never raise.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-024

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-026
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Where the report item can reach the network
STATEMENT: >>>
The report item shall make outbound requests only from `fetch_weather` (Open-Meteo, 2.0 s timeout per request,
at most two requests), `reverse_geocode` (Nominatim, 2.0 s timeout, one request) and the `AIEnhancer` provider
calls (Groq or Anthropic, 30 s timeout, 2 retries). These functions do not read the offline setting themselves;
the caller keeps offline mode by not calling them.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The tests replace `urlopen` and the provider call; none checks that no other module opens a connection. A review
searches the item's files for `urllib`, `socket`, `requests`, `httpx`, `openai` and `anthropic`. Offline mode
itself is tested with the orchestrator, which owns the check.
<<<
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-025

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-027
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Airframe name from the parameters
STATEMENT: >>>
The report item shall give the parsers a name for the airframe: for PX4 the name and frame type for a
`SYS_AUTOSTART` id from a table shipped with the package, and for ArduPilot a frame name from `FRAME_CLASS` and
`FRAME_TYPE` (`Q_FRAME_CLASS`/`Q_FRAME_TYPE` for a quadplane, `FRAME_CONFIG` for a submarine), by vehicle type.
An unknown id or missing parameters give no name.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No system requirement asks for an airframe name; it fills `FlightMetadata.airframe_name` for the reader.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: report
DERIVED: Yes
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-RPT-028
STATUS: Active
TITLE: One text form for UTC times, and a floor for a set clock
STATEMENT: >>>
The report item shall give the parsers one function that turns a UTC epoch time in microseconds into the text
`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ` (whole seconds, truncated) used for `log_start_utc`, and one constant,
1 262 304 000 000 000 us (2010-01-01T00:00:00Z), below which a clock is taken as never set.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test in this item's files calls `utc_iso`; the parser tests use it through `log_start_utc`. A review checks
the format string and the constant.
<<<
ALLOCATION: report
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-024

